REASON
Em dash cleanup (workspace rule: no em dashes in any project). Each U+2014 is rewritten by context: a colon for an explanation or list, a comma before a conjunction (and, but, which...) or when the clause already has a colon, parentheses for a paired aside, a hyphen for an empty value (table cells, placeholders). Sentences the first pass garbled were corrected by hand after two features-validator reviews. No wording or behaviour change otherwise.

OLD_SECTION (line 16)
The page is held with `overflow` rather than by taking the body out of flow, so the document never moves: the scroll position is preserved because nothing scrolled, not because it was saved and reapplied. Two consequences worth knowing [em dash] the page behind keeps its normal layout while a modal is up, and `overflow: hidden` blocks *user* scrolling (wheel, touch, keyboard) but not programmatic `scrollTo()`, so your own code can still move the page behind a modal if it chooses to.
