OLD_SECTION (line 34)
Page-level state is handled at the stack boundary rather than per modal. The body is frozen and the scroll position captured when the first layer opens, and released only when the last layer closes [em dash] so nesting never loses the page's scroll position. Similarly a blurred `pageContainer` stays blurred until no remaining layer wants it blurred.
NEW_SECTION (line 34)
Page-level state is handled at the stack boundary rather than per modal. The body is frozen and the scroll position captured when the first layer opens, and released only when the last layer closes, so nesting never loses the page's scroll position. Similarly a blurred `pageContainer` stays blurred until no remaining layer wants it blurred.
